WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.358
Object detection identifies configured categories and their locations in a frame.

00:00:05.358 --> 00:00:10.716
Image classification assigns a label to an image or cropped region.

00:00:10.716 --> 00:00:18.646
Scene-description models generate natural-language summaries, while activity-recognition systems examine change across time rather than a single picture.

00:00:18.646 --> 00:00:23.576
Vision-language models can answer broader questions about images or clips.

00:00:23.576 --> 00:00:31.934
Their flexibility is useful for review and summarization, but output can vary with wording, model version, and context.

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:36.435
A fluent description is not necessarily a correct one.

00:00:36.435 --> 00:00:43.936
A false positive occurs when the system reports an event that did not happen as described.

00:00:43.936 --> 00:00:48.866
A false negative occurs when a relevant event is missed.

00:00:48.866 --> 00:00:55.081
Both matter: excessive false alerts create fatigue, while missed events create misplaced confidence.

00:00:55.081 --> 00:01:03.440
Lighting, weather, shadows, camera angle, distance, occlusion, dirty lenses, compression, frame rate, and motion blur can change results.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:11.798
Models also face domain shift when the local scene differs from their training data or changes over time.

00:01:11.798 --> 00:01:16.299
Confidence values are model-specific signals, not guarantees of truth.

00:01:16.299 --> 00:01:19.514
Thresholds trade sensitivity against false alerts.

00:01:19.514 --> 00:01:27.444
Evaluate performance with representative local footage, including daytime, night, seasons, common objects, and unusual but legitimate activity.

00:01:27.444 --> 00:01:33.659
Treat AI output as assistance, not proof of identity, intent, wrongdoing, or safety.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:39.875
Preserve context for authorized human review, document limitations, and avoid high-consequence automatic action.

00:01:39.875 --> 00:01:45.233
Responsible use begins by admitting what the model cannot reliably know.
